TITLE:: ActionMenu
SUMMARY:: A Button with a popup list window for performing actions.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMlib,  Classes/PathActionMenu,  Classes/ListView

DESCRIPTION::
A Button with a Popup List for performing actions.
Closes on unfocus or with esc key.

Supports Button, SmoothButton, or RoundButton (RECOMMENDED) as button classes.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create an ActionMenu

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect

ARGUMENT:: name
The Menu Button Title

ARGUMENT:: items
An Array of Strings or Associations (\key->function)

ARGUMENT:: showArrow
show a little down-tick arrow, defaults to true

returns::
an ActionMenu


METHOD:: buttonClass
Default: Button

but you can use the SmoothButton or RoundButton  (RECOMMENDED) from the wonderful wslib quark.


returns:: the Button class.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: defaultAction
a function. if you a add only a string, not an association, this function will be used.


METHOD:: fontSize


METHOD:: button
the menu Button


METHOD:: globalAction
a global function to be evaluated on selection

returns:: (describe returnvalue here)

METHOD:: closeOnSelect
default Boolean is true. Close the select window after selection.

METHOD:: unfocusClose
default Boolean is true. Close the select on unfocs (click outside).

METHOD:: toolTip
set a tooltip for the menu button



PRIVATE:: prAddSpacer
PRIVATE:: removeAt
PRIVATE:: items
PRIVATE:: doActionAt
PRIVATE:: makeButton
PRIVATE:: name
PRIVATE:: prButtonAction
PRIVATE:: prGetWinBounds
PRIVATE:: prMakeListView
PRIVATE:: prAddItem
PRIVATE:: prSetWinPosition
PRIVATE:: value
PRIVATE:: valueIndexName
PRIVATE:: valueName
PRIVATE:: pr_makeAction
EXAMPLES::

code::
(
w = Window.new("ActionMenu Examples").front;
w.flow{arg w;
    var b;
    ActionMenu(w,Rect(0,0,80,25),"Vocalize",[
        \sing ->{"sing".postln},
        \shout ->{"shout".postln},
        \grunt ->{"grunt".postln},
    ]);

    // prevent closing, use a separator
    b=ActionMenu(w,Rect(0,0,80,25),"No Close").closeOnSelect_(false);
    b.items_(
        [
            \sing ->{"sing".postln},
            "-", // separator. no action
            \shout ->{"shout".postln},
    ]).unfocusClose_(false); // don't close when clicked outside

    // Chosen value shown on button label; Use a globalAction.
    b=ActionMenu(w,Rect(0,0,80,25),"Select",["fast","medium","slow"]).globalAction_{|val|
        b.button.states[0][0]=val.asString;
        b.button.refresh;
        b.button.focus(0);
    };
    w.startRow;
    StaticText(w,Rect(0,0,200,40)).string_("Click outside to close.");
    w.startRow;
    StaticText(w,Rect(0,0,200,40)).string_("Escape key  to close.");


}
)

::
